From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:22:21 +0200
Subject: nv30: the small-surface hack's window clip stays inside the block it
 draws

nv30_validate_fb draws a swizzled render target whose offset is not 64-aligned (a 2x2 mip level
at half a cache line, 16 bpp) as a 16x2 swizzled block, moving the window origin right by the
offset's remainder (x = 8 for a 2x2 R5G6B5 at offset & 63 = 32) to land on the real pixels. The
window clip stayed at the block's whole width (max 15), so origin plus clip spanned x more
columns than the block: 24 against 16. The draw is inside the 2x2 by the viewport and scissor,
but a rule that bounds a draw by origin plus clip (ps3rsx's, P4 slice c1) can't know that, and
Armagetron's draws were refused.

In that hack the window clip is now what is left of the block after the origin: w - x columns
(max 7 for x = 8), so origin plus clip is the block's width. Every other target keeps its clip
(the render target's size), the linear unaligned-offset case included, which grows its width the
other way (w += x) and is left alone.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state_validate.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state_validate.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state_validate.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state_validate.c
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@ nv30_validate_fb(struct nv30_context *nv30)
    int w = fb->width;
    int x = 0;
    int y = 0;
+   int clip_w = -1;	/* the window clip's width, when it is not the render target's (the small-surface hack) */
 
    nv30->state.rt_enable = (NV30_3D_RT_ENABLE_COLOR0 << fb->nr_cbufs) - 1;
    if (nv30->state.rt_enable > 1)
@@ -99,9 +100,15 @@ nv30_validate_fb(struct nv30_context *nv30)
          x += off / (util_format_get_blocksize(nv30->fb_cbufs[0]->format) * 2);
          w  = 16;
          h  = 2;
+         /* the 2x2 is drawn as a 16-wide swizzled block from the window origin x: a window clip of
+          * the block's whole width would reach x columns past it. Clip to what is left of the block. */
+         clip_w = MAX2(w - x, 1);
       }
    }
 
+   if (clip_w < 0)
+      clip_w = w;
+
    if (rt_format & NV30_3D_RT_FORMAT_TYPE_SWIZZLED) {
       rt_format |= util_logbase2(w) << 16;
       rt_format |= util_logbase2(h) << 24;
@@ -123,7 +130,7 @@ nv30_validate_fb(struct nv30_context *nv30)
    BEGIN_NV04(push, NV30_3D(VIEWPORT_TX_ORIGIN), 4);
    PUSH_DATA (push, (y << 16) | x);
    PUSH_DATA (push, 0);
-   PUSH_DATA (push, ((w - 1) << 16) | 0);
+   PUSH_DATA (push, ((clip_w - 1) << 16) | 0);
    PUSH_DATA (push, ((h - 1) << 16) | 0);
 
    if ((nv30->state.rt_enable & NV30_3D_RT_ENABLE_COLOR0) || fb->zsbuf.texture) {
